From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 11:24:59 +0200
Subject: usb: typec: ucsi: glink: Set initial orientation during probe

The connector orientation GPIO and the Type-C switches are available
before the UCSI PPM provided by the ADSP is running. However, the driver
only propagates the GPIO state from connector_status(), which is not
called until the PPM has started and UCSI registration has completed.

When a device is connected in reverse orientation during boot, USB
enumeration can therefore start before the orientation switches have been
configured. This results in repeated USB protocol errors until the ADSP
starts and the orientation is eventually propagated.

Acquire the switches and propagate the GPIO state while probing each
connector. This configures the orientation before USB enumeration while
retaining connector_status() for subsequent connection state changes.
Defer probing if an associated switch has not registered yet.

Fixes: c6165ed2f425 ("usb: ucsi: glink: use the connector orientation GPIO to provide switch events")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>

(cherry picked from commit d2360e56a23ebf0c18cc5761e11e3db5457783a6)
[SuperKali: forward-ported from radxa/kernel linux-7.0.11 to Linux 7.2.3]
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c | 37 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
@@ -238,6 +238,38 @@ static const struct ucsi_operations pmic_glink_ucsi_ops = {
 	.connector_status = pmic_glink_ucsi_connector_status,
 };
 
+static int pmic_glink_ucsi_set_initial_orientation(struct device *dev,
+						   struct fwnode_handle *fwnode,
+						   struct gpio_desc *desc)
+{
+	struct typec_switch *sw;
+	int orientation;
+	int ret;
+
+	sw = fwnode_typec_switch_get(fwnode);
+	if (IS_ERR(sw))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(sw),
+				     "failed to acquire orientation switch\n");
+
+	orientation = gpiod_get_value(desc);
+	if (orientation < 0) {
+		ret = orientation;
+		goto out_put_switch;
+	}
+
+	ret = typec_switch_set(sw, orientation ? TYPEC_ORIENTATION_REVERSE :
+						 TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NORMAL);
+
+out_put_switch:
+	typec_switch_put(sw);
+
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "failed to set initial orientation\n");
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static void pmic_glink_ucsi_read_ack(struct pmic_glink_ucsi *ucsi, const void *data, int len)
 {
 	u32 ret_code, resp_len, buf_len = 0;
@@ -449,6 +481,11 @@ static int pmic_glink_ucsi_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 					     "unable to acquire orientation gpio\n");
 
 		ucsi->port_orientation[port] = desc;
+
+		/* The orientation GPIO is available before the PPM is running. */
+		ret = pmic_glink_ucsi_set_initial_orientation(dev, fwnode, desc);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 	}
 
 	ucsi->client = devm_pmic_glink_client_alloc(dev, PMIC_GLINK_OWNER_USBC,
-- 
Armbian

